# Decisions - tb-convergence-severity-calibration

**Feature start:** 2026-11-27

Permanent decision records promoted from `scratchpad.md` and `interview.md` at
PR boundaries. Goal autonomy: every agent entry below was decided on the
human's behalf and is listed on the PR for Trent to check.

## DEC-1. Full rigor, goal autonomy

- **Answered by:** human
- **Decision:** Full rigor with goal autonomy (relayed from the coordinating
  thread). Planning decisions are `autonomous-evaluator` decisions citing
  independent planning reviews: design (Codex, round 5 FAIL settled by
  recorded judgment, DEC-6) and spec (Codex, round 2 PASS).
- **Source:** scratchpad S1.

## DEC-2. Severity calibration is instruction text, likelihood first

- **Answered by:** agent
- **Decision:** Code and planning reviewer instructions judge likelihood
  before consequence. Realistic means ordinary use within the handled
  conditions with no one acting unusually; two or more independent uncommon
  conditions at once make a finding low whatever its consequence. No schema
  field and no mechanical downgrade.
- **Alternatives:** a `conditions` field with automatic downgrade (schema
  owned by #142; meaning-changing correction).
- **Reversibility:** high; versioned instruction text.
- **Source:** interview D1.

## DEC-3. Reviewers read the failure model from the requirement document

- **Answered by:** agent
- **Decision:** The instructions name the `Failure model` section of
  `spec.md` (or `brief.md`); no packet field. Out-of-model triggers are low;
  failures of the stated refusal behaviour are in the model; without the
  section nothing is low for being out of model.
- **Alternatives:** a `packet.failureModel` field (packet assembly owned by
  #142).
- **Reversibility:** high.
- **Source:** interview D2, D6.

## DEC-4. Section check and unbounded-wording lint

- **Answered by:** agent
- **Decision:** A level-2 `## Failure model` section, nonempty, no `TODO`.
  The D11 word list on AC and rubric lines, outside code, unless the same line
  carries "failure model", a numeral (requirement identifiers excluded) or a
  bounding phrase (`at most`, `at least`, `up to`, `no more than`,
  `within`). One diagnostic lists every line.
- **Alternatives:** block-level bounds; a narrower word list.
- **Reversibility:** high; one constant each.
- **Source:** interview D3, D4; scratchpad S4.

## DEC-5. Grandfathering follows exact spec bytes or a resumption's implementation approval

- **Answered by:** agent
- **Decision:** Policy `planning-facts/2`. A spec whose exact bytes were
  validated in the run under the earlier policy, or already grandfathered,
  gets the rules as warnings; so does the spec `run.resume-current` validates
  with a `planning.implementation` approval naming the current commitments.
  Every other spec, including a rewritten one in an old run or a design-only
  resumption, is held to the rules.
- **Alternatives:** grandfather the whole run; hold resumed runs to the rule;
  an opt-in marker; a date cutoff.
- **Reversibility:** medium.
- **Source:** interview D5; scratchpad S3.

## DEC-6. Design approved by judgment at planning round 5

- **Answered by:** agent
- **Decision:** After five design review rounds, the last finding contested
  D11's settled resumed-run warning (which round 4 required). Approved under
  `autonomous-evaluator` authority with a recorded judgment and accepted
  residual risk (a resumption approval that misstates what the human
  approved), narrowed by DEC-5.
- **Alternatives:** park at the round 6 hand-back.
- **Reversibility:** high.
- **Source:** scratchpad S2.

## DEC-7. Documentation bar for light runs only

- **Answered by:** agent
- **Decision:** Light-run reviewer instructions add a "good enough" bar:
  documentation findings block only when following the text as written leads
  to a wrong or unsafe outcome; wording and completeness polish is low; the
  bar never lowers what the brief asks for. Full runs are unchanged.
- **Alternatives:** demote `*.md` findings mechanically; one reviewer for
  docs-only changes; apply the bar in full runs too.
- **Reversibility:** high.
- **Source:** interview D7.

## DEC-8. Review contract version moves; builders exported for tests

- **Answered by:** agent
- **Decision:** `REVIEW_CONTRACT_VERSION` becomes
  `gatereeve-review/2026-11-c2` so in-flight runs keep retained qualification.
  `evaluatorInstructions` and `planningInstructions` are exported for tests.
- **Alternatives:** keep the version (forces re-review on upgrade).
- **Reversibility:** high; expect a trivial merge conflict with #142.
- **Source:** interview D8; scratchpad S5.
